//! check: fail(E0107)
//! phase: none
//! conforms: type.int.not, gram.expr.prec
//!
//! s252 (wolf-lang#800, yew G11): by design. wolf's bitwise not is the
//! prefix `!` on an integer (`[type.int.not]`, ruling #51: `!` on
//! integers, over a `~` operator), so `~2 & flags` is the stray
//! character E0107 — whose report since s252 names `!` and offers the
//! machine-applicable edit to `!2 & flags`, which prints `5` here
//! (`int_not_mask.lu` holds the idioms). yew's port had written
//! `v - (v & m)` for the missing operator it had not found. lupin
//! 0.1.54: E0107 too.

fn main() {
    let flags = 7
    let cleared = ~2 & flags
    print("{cleared}")
}
